{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_24","type":"agent_message","text":"Implemented all `unimplemented!()` bodies in [src/xopt.rs](/tmp/harvest-crust-aPpc4v/project/src/xopt.rs) and [src/snprintf.rs](/tmp/harvest-crust-aPpc4v/project/src/snprintf.rs).\n\nThe main work was translating the `xopt.c` parser semantics into Rust: context creation, extras collection, `--` handling, condensed short options, strict/POSIX checks, autohelp formatting, and offset-based default assignment. That last part required a small amount of `unsafe` pointer arithmetic because the Rust API keeps the original C-style `offset` contract.\n\nI also filled in the exposed `snprintf` compatibility functions with a safe Rust implementation that covers the project’s formatting needs and provides sensible behavior for the helper routines.\n\nVerification: `cargo build` succeeds. No `unimplemented!()`, `todo!()`, or `panic!()` remain in `src/`."}}
